ut tim kaine who ran alongside  hillary in 2016. it is difficult to  imagine a less exciting  and more milk toast candidate than tim  kaine i i feel almost embarrassed to  even mention the idea of tim kaine as  the nominee  um  it's it's very tough to imagine that's  the direction so i don't see any strong  candidates right now a few things i will  mention on rhetoric and what i mean by  that is  in terms of being able to mix it up with  people effectively in media and in  debates um and come up with sort of like  snappy comebacks and and optics  there's something interesting about pete  but edge edge  but he's already suffered and been the  target of significant character  assassination in his role as secretary  of department of transportation  secretary of transportation you don't  typically see that  secretary of transportation  into presidential candidate it's unclear  what his fate would be so i'm just not  sure about it and then it has to be said  that on policy elizabeth warren is one  of the most left candidates of anybody  who's recently run other than bernie her  wealth tax proposal is something to the  left of what most democratic candidates  have proposed but  on a personality personality level the  country really does not seem to like  elizabeth warren so that doesn't seem  particularly good either so  it's a very tough situation  let's get through the midterms insofar  as what happens will inform what the  dynamics of 2024 might be  but i am not particularly optimistic  about the farm team right now  i'm open to having my mind changed let  me know what you think  even if like me you're not vegan and  you're not vegetarian  eating a more plant-based diet is a  really great thing to do for a number of  different reasons and our sponsor just  egg is the delicious plant-based egg you  can use it anywhere you use traditional  eggs because the taste and texture are  identical but just eggplant-based eggs  have the same amount of protein as  traditional eggs 